# Example State @state
> A made-up state, used to show every construct the format has.
region

## Statewide @statewide

### Governor @governor
contest, partisan
note: Open seat.

+ Alice Alvarez (Democratic)
* Bob Brown (Republican)
- Carol Chen (Independent): perennial candidate
  Ran in 2018 and 2022 and lost both times.

Alvarez has the record. See [the Senate race](@senate) for why the pairing
matters, and *read the fine print* on **both** bonds below.

### State Senate, District 3 @senate
contest, partisan, write-ins

+ Dana Dubois (write-in)
- Eve Evans (Democratic, incumbent)

Evans is the only name printed; write in Dubois.

## Example City @city
> City elections use ranked choice for single seats.
region

### Mayor @mayor
contest, ranked, rank up to 3

1. Frank Fox: small business owner
2. Grace Garcia: council member
2. Hank Hill: school board trustee
- Ivy Ito

Fox first. Garcia and Hill are interchangeable for the remaining spots.

### School Board @school-board
contest, 2 seats, unverified

* Jo Jones
* Kim Kaur
* Lee Lopez

vote: undecided

### City Treasurer @treasurer
contest

* Max Moore
* Nia Nkemelu

vote: none

Both are fine. Vote for whoever you like.

### Measure A @measure-a
> Parks bond
measure
placed by: City Council, unanimous
yes: Authorizes $50 million in bonds for park maintenance.
no: Keeps park funding at current levels.
threshold: two-thirds
supporters: Friends of the Parks, the Chamber of Commerce
opponents: Taxpayers United
vote: yes

Cheap money for a real backlog. The \*literal asterisk\* is escaped here.

### Measure B @measure-b
> Sales tax increase
measure
yes: Raises the sales tax by a quarter cent for ten years.
vote: undecided

### Judge Olivia Ortiz @ortiz
retention
designation: Superior Court Judge
vote: yes
